{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-05-12T02:08:44.225Z","tool_name":"run_shell_command","tool_id":"run_shell_command_1778551724225_0","parameters":{"description":"Create README files for papers, datasets, and code directories, and setup .gitignore for datasets.","command":"# Create papers/README.md\ncat > papers/README.md << 'EOF'\n# Downloaded Papers\n\n1. [DialDefer: A Framework for Detecting and Mitigating LLM Dialogic Deference](2601.10896v1_DialDefer_A_Framework_for_Detecting_and_Mitigating_LLM_Dialogic_Deference.pdf)\n   - Authors: Parisa Rabbani et al.\n   - Year: 2026\n   - arXiv: 2601.10896\n   - Why relevant: Introduces DDS metric for framing-induced judgment shifts.\n\n2. [Diagnosing and Mitigating Sycophancy and Skepticism in LLM Causal Judgment](2601.08258v3_Diagnosing_and_Mitigating_Sycophancy_and_Skepticism_in_LLM_Causal_Judgment.pdf)\n   - Authors: Edward Y. Chang\n   - Year: 2026\n   - arXiv: 2601.08258\n   - Why relevant: Identifies skepticism and sycophancy traps in reasoning.\n\n3. [Challenging the Evaluator: LLM Sycophancy Under User Rebuttal](2509.16533v1_Challenging_the_Evaluator_LLM_Sycophancy_Under_User_Rebuttal.pdf)\n   - Authors: Sungwon Kim, Daniel Khashabi\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: 2509.16533\n   - Why relevant: Studies sycophancy when challenged by users.\n\n4. [Justice or Prejudice? Quantifying Biases in LLM-as-a-Judge](2410.02736v2_Justice_or_Prejudice_Quantifying_Biases_in_LLM-as-a-Judge.pdf)\n   - Authors: Jiayi Ye et al.\n   - Year: 2024\n   - arXiv: 2410.02736\n   - Why relevant: Comprehensive list of judgment biases (CALM).\nEOF\n\n# Create datasets/README.md\ncat > datasets/README.md << 'EOF'\n# Datasets for Experimentation\n\nNote: Actual data files are located in the `code/` directory repositories but summarized here.\n\n## 1. DialDefer Unified Benchmark\n- **Location**: `code/DialDefer/dataset/benchmark_data/sampled_formatted/`\n- **Source**: AdvisorQA, TruthfulQA, GPQA, etc.\n- **Task**: Factual inquiry vs. Conversational judgment.\n\n## 2. r/AIO (Am I Overreacting)\n- **Location**: `code/DialDefer/dataset/aio/`\n- **Source**: Reddit naturalistic conversations.\n- **Task**: Interpersonal conflict judgment.\n\n## 3. CausalT3 / CausalT5K\n- **Location**: `code/CausalT5kBench/final_dataset/`\n- **Source**: Causal reasoning vignettes across 10 domains.\n- **Task**: Causal link verification under pressure.\n\n## 4. CALM Bias Datasets\n- **Location**: `code/LLM-Judge-Bias-Dataset/bias_datasets/`\n- **Source**: Perturbed datasets for Authority, Verbosity, Sentiment biases.\n- **Task**: Bias quantification in LLM judgments.\nEOF\n\n# Create code/README.md\ncat > code/README.md << 'EOF'\n# Cloned Repositories\n\n## 1. DialDefer\n- URL: https://github.com/LadyPary/DialDefer\n- Purpose: Framework for detecting \"Dialogic Deference\" using DDS metric.\n- Location: `code/DialDefer/`\n\n## 2. CausalT5kBench\n- URL: https://github.com/genglongling/CausalT5kBench\n- Purpose: Large-scale causal reasoning benchmark with expert-annotated traps.\n- Location: `code/CausalT5kBench/`\n\n## 3. LLM-Judge-Bias-Dataset\n- URL: https://github.com/Y0oMu/LLM-Judge-Bias-Dataset\n- Purpose: Datasets and prompt templates for the CALM bias quantification framework.\n- Location: `code/LLM-Judge-Bias-Dataset/`\nEOF\n\n# Create .gitignore for datasets\ncat > datasets/.gitignore << 'EOF'\n# Exclude all data files\n*\n\n# But include documentation\n!.gitignore\n!README.md\nEOF\n"}}
